    <abstract><!-- can be changed via merge in the assembly -->
      <para>
       Linux kernel's scheduler allocates processor execution time to running threads according to process-level CPU scheduling policies.
      </para>
    </abstract>
  </info>
  <section xml:id="rt-cpu-scheduling-policies-types">
    <title>Scheduling Policies</title>
    <para>
      The Linux kernel scheduler can use the following policies:
    </para>
    <variablelist>
    <varlistentry>
    <term><literal>SCHED_FIFO</literal></term>
    <listitem>
    <para><emphasis role="bold">First In, First Out</emphasis>: A running thread continues executing until it blocks on an I/O request, explicitly yields execution, or is preempted by a higher-priority real-time thread. Priority levels range from 1 (lowest) to 99 (highest).</para>
    </listitem>
    </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </section>
